  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Compound Chain Rule is not about memorising a giant fraction.\n\nIt is about one target. Pick what you are trying to find, then ask how every other changing quantity pushes that target: up or down.\n\nDirection first. Arithmetic second.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Suppose 5 workers collect 60 kg in 3 days. We want the quantity collected by 8 workers in 5 days.\n\nTarget = quantity.\nMore workers → more quantity: direct.\nMore days → more quantity: direct.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "So quantity scales by 8/5 × 5/3.\n60 × 8/5 × 5/3 = 160 kg.\n\nThe two direction decisions explain the entire setup.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
